A||N||6||Calab52||Rear Speakers||||11||
Z||000000||Calab52||09-23-2001||10:51 PM||||What is the best way to remove/replace the rear speakers without breaking the covers,etc.?||||reg||11
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-24-2001||12:35 AM||||The "covers" on the rear speakers dont come off. You have to take the entire inner panel off. Its pretty easy..take off the seatbelt bolt (t-47 torx if memory serves)...then I think theres a screw on the side (you have to open the door to see it)..then CAREFULLY pry off the inner panel...you'll probobly break the retaining clips that hold the panel on...it happens. Most auto parts places carry similar replacements. Once you get it off you'll see the speaker...remove as normal from that point on.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||09-24-2001||03:25 PM||||While this thread is open, I would like to hear from others what brand and model speakers they have installed in this spot.<BR>My pioneer 4X6's are starting to pop and I remember it was hard to find some that fit properly. I don't want to do that trial and error thing again. Thanks to all who reply!<BR>Terry ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dgzfiero||09-24-2001||03:45 PM|||| I can't remember the models but I am running 4x10coaxial Alpines up front and 4x6 plates in the back also by Alpine. They' getting fed either 40 or 50 watts and I ain't blew 'em up yet. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||recluse||09-24-2001||05:04 PM||||I have infinity Reference 4x6 plates (4" round and separate tweeter).  I am very happy with the sound. I plan on getting some Infinitys for the front too.  Check with Crutchfield.com they have many different 4x6 speakers.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Oreif||09-24-2001||08:41 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by recluse:<BR><B>I have infinity Reference 4x6 plates (4" round and separate tweeter).  I am very happy with the sound. I plan on getting some Infinitys for the front too.  Check with Crutchfield.com they have many different 4x6 speakers.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Infinity plates use a 3 1/2" woofer not a 4". All 4 X 6 plates use a 3 1/2" woofer except ADS, but ADS won't fit due to the size and placement of the 4" woofer. The 4" woofer needs to be centered in the hole for the magnet to fit. I put in 4" woofers with a seperate 1" tweeter in my sail panels. The tweeter is mounted high up angling down for balance and direction. Since I used the same speakers in the front and a seperate 8" subwoofer there is no popping with the bass (controlled by the crossover) and it sounds excellent! I even have digital surround sound.(See pics below)<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sail_4.jpg">   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tcleand.jpg">   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Speaker_set.jpg">   <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">      <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||varnster||09-24-2001||08:51 PM||||I put the infinity ref plates in, with 4x6<BR>infinity kapa for the front, and a 8" JL AUDIO micro sub for the bass. sounds very clean no pop, only pleasure ear candy! AS <BR>close as the rears are you dont have to get<BR>to crazy just something that will handle your amp, their mostly for fill anyway.The <BR>statement above was to see how many people<BR>will disagree with me before I log off.||||reg||7
